  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2}-7 & =2 \\\\ {e}^{x+2} & =2+7 \\\\ {e}^{x+2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2} & =9 \\\\ ln\u2061({e}^{x+2}) & =ln\u2061(9) \\\\ x+2 & =ln\u2061(9) \\\\ x & =ln\u2061(9)-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\u22480.197\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
